  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 42a7ef911f4c60e408989a759d2b9b18, type: 3}
  m_Name: PY_ARITHMETIC
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.LessonData
  id: PY_ARITHMETIC
  language: 1
  conceptTitle: Arithmetic Operators
  symbol: + - * /
  relatedQuestionIds:
  - PY_03_ARITHMETIC
  topics:
  - Arithmetic
  definition: Arithmetic operators are symbols that let a program do maths with numbers.
  howItWorks: '+ adds, - subtracts and * multiplies. Python has three kinds of division:
    / gives the exact answer with a decimal, // keeps only the whole-number part
    (floor division), and % gives the remainder that is left over.'
  exampleCode: 'cookies = 9

    print(cookies / 2)

    print(cookies // 2)

    print(cookies
    % 2)'
  exampleExplanation: '9 / 2 is 4.5. 9 // 2 keeps only the whole part, 4. 9 % 2 is
    the remainder: 9 shared into two equal piles is 4 each, with 1 left over, so
    it prints 1.'
  tip: 'Python follows maths rules: * and / are worked out before + and -.'
